  "version": 2,
  "_readme": "Maps Excel column field keys (from sheet_experiment.py) to NOMAD archive JSON paths per process type, for live batch-template autofill. AUTHORITATIVE SOURCE (2026-07-15): this app's process types are ingested by NOMAD's own parser/mapper, which is the ground truth for archive field names - not the sample archive JSON dumps used earlier in this file's history (those only show what happened to be filled in one batch, not the full schema, and are easy to under-map from). Parser (routes Excel column headers -> per-process-type mapper by substring match): https://github.com/nomad-hzb/nomad-hysprint/blob/main/src/nomad_hysprint/parsers/hysprint_batch_parser.py . Field-by-field mapper (the map_<process_type> functions - this is where every archive path below was read from): https://github.com/nomad-hzb/nomad-baseclasses/blob/main/src/baseclasses/helper/solar_cell_batch_mapping.py . HOW TO UPDATE (both repos are actively developed upstream): (1) refetch both URLs above (raw.githubusercontent.com/.../main/... works without auth), (2) find the map_<type> function for the process type you're touching, (3) for each field you want, note the Excel column string passed to get_value(data, <key>, ...) - if <key> is a list, that's several ALTERNATIVE Excel spellings NOMAD's parser accepts, not several archive paths - and the archive attribute path being assigned into (a Python object's constructor kwarg name / attribute name, which the archive JSON serializes under that exact same key), (4) cross-check the Excel column string actually appears in apps/Excel_creator/sheet_experiment.py's generate_steps_for_process for that process type - if it doesn't, this app never generates that column, so don't bother mapping it (harmless if you do - it'll just never match a real field_spec - but it's noise), (5) add/edit the entry here; nothing in data_manager.py needs to change. 'path' is a list of dict keys / list indices walked in order. A field may instead use 'paths' (plural) - a list of ALTERNATIVE full archive paths tried in order, first non-None wins - for the cases (Evaporation, see below) where the archive stores the same field under a different parent key depending on data this app doesn't itself track (an 'Organic'/co-evaporation flag) - same field names inside, different list name. 'unit_verified: false' means the value is copied from the archive with NO unit conversion applied and has NOT been confirmed to match the Excel column's stated unit - check against the NOMAD web GUI, then flip to true, before trusting that field's autofill; string fields have no unit concept and are unit_verified: true. 'indexed_fields' generate one entry per n in 'range' (inclusive); '{i}' inside path_template (or path_templates, plural, same alternative-paths idea) is the 0-based list index (n - 1), '{n}' inside excel_key_template is the 1-based Excel column suffix. An indexed_fields entry may optionally carry a 'config_key' (e.g. 'solvents', 'solutes', 'spinsteps', 'materials') - tag exactly one representative entry per config concept; data_manager.infer_config_from_source_step uses it to widen a target process's config to match how much data a source batch step actually has. NOTE on process-type naming: the real archive's 'method' field doesn't always match this app's AVAILABLE_PROCESSES labels 1:1 (e.g. real 'Atomic Layer Deposition' vs this app's 'ALD', or a single real 'Cleaning' step covering what this app models as two separate types 'Cleaning O2-Plasma'/'Cleaning UV-Ozone') - see data_manager.resolve_process_type, which translates before these paths are looked up, so the keys below are still this app's own process type names, not the raw archive method string. Deliberately NOT mapped yet: Ink Recycling (separate mapper file, nomad_hysprint.parsers.file_parser.ink_recycling_mappers.map_ink_recycling, not yet fetched), Sublimation (the real parser's parse() only substring-matches 'evaporation' in the column header, never 'sublimation' - Sublimation columns appear to have no real archive ingestion path at all despite sheet_experiment.py treating it like Evaporation client-side). An optional 'multiply' key (field entries and indexed_fields entries) applies a confirmed numeric unit-conversion factor to the raw archive value before it's written/previewed (data_manager.FIELD_VALUE_MULTIPLIERS/_apply_multiplier) - only add it once verified against the actual NOMAD quantity definition, not guessed, same discipline as unit_verified. Example added 2026-07-28: Cleaning's shared CleaningTechnique.time quantity is declared unit='minute' in nomad-baseclasses/material_processes_misc/cleaning.py, but this app's Excel columns for it ('Time {n} [s]', 'UV-Ozone Time [s]', 'Gas-Plasma Time [s]') are labeled seconds - confirmed live against real batch HZB_IJP_Green Ink_6_1 (a real value of 15 = 15 minutes, previously copied unconverted into a '[s]' column) - so those three carry 'multiply': 60 and are now unit_verified: true. The 'Experiment Info' entry below is a special case: its 'path' segments index into a synthetic {'sample': <HySprint_Sample data>, 'substrate': <HySprint_Substrate data>} dict (see data_manager.fetch_experiment_info_source), not a process step from get_processing_steps, since these fields live on the sample/substrate entities rather than a process. Date/Project_Name/Batch/Subbatch are deliberately never autofilled even though 'Experiment Info' has other mapped fields - see EXPERIMENT_INFO_NEVER_AUTOFILLED in data_manager.py. 'Sample dimension' has no known NOMAD archive source and is deliberately left unmapped. Update 2026-07-29 (verified live against real batch HZB_ThNa_1_1 / upload WIMzMde-TeqKv6RyanapOw): 'Sheet Resistance [Ohms/square]' and 'Transmission [%]' were always returning None because a newer NOMAD schema version moved these two off the substrate entry's flat attributes into a 'substrate_properties' list (one dict per named layer, e.g. layer_type='Substrate Conductive Layer'), same list 'Substrate conductive layer' already reads layer_material_name from at index 0 - the flat 'substrate.layer_sheet_resistance'/'substrate.layer_transmission' paths are kept as the first alternative (older oasis instances / archives created before the schema change may still have them there) with the substrate_properties[0] path added as a fallback, same first-non-None-wins pattern as Evaporation's organic/inorganic split above. If a future real batch has substrate_properties entries where index 0 isn't the conductive layer, this will need matching by layer_type instead of a fixed index - not implemented, since _get_path_any has no key-match capability, only fixed dict/list traversal. Update 2026-07-29 (second pass, cross-checked directly against map_layer/map_solutions in solar_cell_batch_mapping.py, not just archive dumps): added 'Layer thickness [nm]' (path layer[0].layer_thickness) to Spin Coating/Slot Die Coating/Blade Coating - was mapped nowhere despite being a real, always-generated Excel column for every layer-depositing process type. Fixed a real wrong-value bug in 'Solvent {n} name' for those same three process types: the old path solvent[i].name pointed at a NOMAD-computed DISPLAY string that concatenates the chemical name with its volume and unit (e.g. 'DMF 0.01 milliliter'), not the plain chemical name the Excel column expects - map_solutions() never sets solvent.name directly, only solvent.chemical_2.name (the actual entered value, e.g. 'DMF'), so the path now points there instead. Added 'Solvent {n} volume [uL]' (chemical_volume), 'Solvent {n} relative amount' (amount_relative), 'Solvent {n} chemical ID' (chemical_id), and 'Solute {n} chemical ID' (solute[i].chemical_id) - all real Excel columns with real archive homes that were simply never mapped (solute[i].name was already correct as-is, since solutes have no volume to concatenate into their display name, so no equivalent fix needed there). Added Slot Die Coating's 'Air knife angle [°]'/'Air knife gap [cm]'/'Bead volume [mm/s]'/'Drying speed [cm/min]' (all under quenching. - see map_air_knife_gas_quenching; units confirmed matching the Excel column labels exactly in the mapper's own get_value(..., unit=...) calls, no multiply needed). Same solvent/solute gaps (volume/relative amount/chemical ID, and the 'name' display-string bug) also exist in Dip Coating and Inkjet Printing's identical solution/solvent/solute block - deliberately NOT fixed there yet since nobody asked/verified against a real batch for those two; same edit pattern applies if/when needed. Evaporation's 'Organic' Excel column is intentionally NOT in this file's paths at all - do NOT map it to co_evaporation (that archive attribute reflects Evaporation-vs-Co-Evaporation Excel SECTION choice, a completely different concept that happens to also be a bool - see map_evaporation's 'coevaporation' parameter). The real Organic/Inorganic choice is only encoded implicitly by which of organic_evaporation/inorganic_evaporation is the populated list on the step, so per user decision (2026-07-29) it's read back via data_manager._DERIVED_FIELDS (a small process_type -> field_key -> callable registry for fields with no single archive path) instead of a JSON path - see _derive_evaporation_organic, wired into both fetch_process_field_values and build_field_mapping_debug_report. It returns the literal strings 'True'/'False' (matching apps/Excel_creator/sheet_experiment.py's make_label('Organic', True) - the Excel column's own spelling - not a Python bool), so it round-trips through ProcessFieldSpec like any other string field. Also NOT fixable at all: Spin Coating's 'Spin Delay [s]' column - confirmed via direct read of map_spin_coating() that NOMAD's own parser never reads this column into any archive attribute; there is no archive path for it to read back from, this is an upstream parser gap. Cleaning's per-bath 'solvent_2' (cleaning[i].solvent_2.name) initially LOOKED like a second, uncaptured per-bath solvent concept - first pass against upload Ng0kIOldQIiUr_OOvgsf3Q (batch HZB_QuNa_1_1) with 4 distinct 'Solvent {n}' Excel values per Cleaning section returned an identical solvent_2.name ('Hellmanex') for every cleaning[i] entry despite time/temperature correctly varying per entry. That turned out to be a false alarm caused by fetching the archive before NOMAD had fully reprocessed the upload, not a real bug - after the user forced a metadata reprocess of the SAME upload/entry_ids, re-fetching (and re-verified directly through data_manager.fetch_process_field_values, not just a raw archive dump) showed 'Solvent {n}' correctly resolving 4 distinct values per section (Hellmanex/IPA/Ethanol/acetone and hotwater/DMF/DMSO/water). Conclusion: this app's existing Cleaning O2-Plasma/UV-Ozone mapping (cleaning[i].name, already in indexed_fields below) was correct all along - no code or config change was needed. solvent_2 is not a distinct 'second solvent' concept at all; it's just the internal PubChemPureSubstanceSectionCustom wrapper object that map_cleaning() stores the raw entered name in (see solar_cell_batch_mapping.py), which NOMAD then echoes/title-cases up to the parent SolutionCleaning's own '.name' - the same value already captured via the existing path, not additional data. Lesson for next time: if a real batch shows an archive-ingestion result that looks broken/collapsed compared to what was entered, force a metadata reprocess and re-fetch before concluding it's an upstream defect - staging/reprocessing lag can look identical to a real ingestion bug. Update 2026-07-29 (third pass): 'Sample dimension' (Experiment Info) DOES have a real archive home after all, contradicting this file's earlier claim - map_substrate() in solar_cell_batch_mapping.py sets substrate_dimension=get_value(data, 'Sample dimension', ...), confirmed live as 'substrate.substrate_dimension' = '1 cm x 1 cm' on real batch HZB_ThNa_1_1; now mapped. Inkjet Printing got the same Layer thickness/Solvent volume-relative amount-chemical ID/Solute chemical ID/'name' path fix already applied to Blade/Slot Die/Spin Coating (see prior update) - Dip Coating still has the identical gap, still deliberately unfixed pending a real batch to verify against. Generic Process is now mapped too, but NOT via a field_mappings.json path for most of its fields: hysprint_batch_parser.py's map_generic_parameters() stores every Excel column except Notes/Name (including the atmosphere/GB columns, and oddly Datetime/Operator too, as a redundant copy) as a flat process_parameters list of {'name': <Excel column>, 'value_number'|'value_string': <value>} - there is no fixed archive path per column, so 'Room temperature [°C]'/'rel. humidity [%]'/the 6 GB oxygen-water-temperature columns are read back via data_manager._DERIVED_FIELDS (same mechanism as Evaporation's 'Organic'), searching process_parameters by name. Confirmed live against both HZB_ThNa_1_1 (values present) and HZB_QuNa_1_1 (columns left blank, correctly returns nothing) on 2026-07-29. Only 'Name' (-> the step's own 'name' attribute, unprefixed - map_generic() sets name=get_value(data,'Name',...) directly) got a normal path entry below; 'Notes' was deliberately left unmapped for consistency with every other process type in this file, none of which autofill Notes. See schema_coverage.md (same directory) for a per-process-type list of which Excel columns still have no mapping/derivation here at all, generated by diffing this file against sheet_experiment.py's own column generation - regenerate it (script referenced inside) whenever this file changes materially.",

